# Live evals are user-triggered only

The eval suites under `agents/evals/` make **live Gemini/Vertex API calls** — they cost real
quota and take minutes. The agent must NEVER run them on its own initiative, even to
"validate" its own changes.

**Forbidden without an explicit, same-session user instruction:**

- `agents/evals/run_e2e.sh` (any mode except `-l`/`--list`/`--help`)
- `pytest -m eval` — covers `test_e2e_eval.py`, `test_routing_eval.py`,
  `test_expert_eval.py`, `test_verification_eval.py`
- `agents/evals/bench/runner.py` (any benchmark, any `--limit`)
- Any other command that calls a live model API

**Allowed and encouraged instead:**

- Hermetic unit tests (default `pytest`, marker-guarded `-m 'not eval'`) — run freely
- Local docker builds and toolchain smoke tests — run freely
- *Suggesting* an eval run when it would be useful ("recommend running the E2E now —
  `agents/evals/run_e2e.sh`") and letting the user decide

If a task seems to call for an eval run, stop and ask. "Validation" in a plan or todo means
unit tests and local builds unless the user says otherwise.
